ns for B2C transactions, leveraging proprietary software platform, distributed through independent sales organizations, direct sales, and vertically focused independent software vendors channels. It also offers MX product suite, which includes MX Connect and MX Merchant products, which provides flexible and customizable set of business applications that helps to manage critical business work functions and revenue performance using core payment processing. In addition, the company offers CPX, a platform that offers accounts payable automation solutions, including virtual card, purchase card, ACH +, dynamic discounting, or check. Further, it provides accounts payable automation solutions to corporations, software partners and financial institutions, including Citibank, Visa, and Mastercard. Additionally, the company offers embedded finance and BaaS solutions to customers to modernize legacy platforms and accelerate software partners' strategies to monetize payments. It serves SMB and enterprises, as well as distribution partners, including retail and wholesale independent sales organizations, financial institutions, and independent software vendors and value-added resellers. The company was formerly known as Priority Holdings, LLC and changed its name to Priority Technology Holdings, Inc. in July 2018. Priority Technology Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in Alpharetta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Charles Priore | Executive Chairman, President & CEO | Age 56 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $804K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, improving at 19%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $63K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Priority Technology Holdings, I is a small-cap technology business with a $650M market cap on $953M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $75M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.80\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 64% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8857142857142851},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 78% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 49% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in PRTH Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_PRTH_Response_110626070002_1793966402.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793966402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Priority Technology (PRTH) Lags Q3 Earnings Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024242/priority-technology-prth-lags-q3-earnings-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024242","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885706.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (PRTH) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_PRTH_Edition_102726071602_1793099762.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793099762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are PRTH, BWIN, CCC Obtaining Fair Deals for their Shareholders?","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/are-prth-bwin-ccc-obtaining-fa